---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service">
  <nav class="nav">
    <div class="nav-inner nav-inner-narrow">
      <a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">🐚</span> Conchquest</a>
      <a class="back" href="/">← Back to home</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="wrap page-wrap">
    <div class="draft-flag">
      <strong>Draft — not yet reviewed by an attorney.</strong> This is a starter template written to match Conchquest's
      actual features (location data, crowdsourced photos, subscriptions). Have a lawyer review before this goes live,
      especially the sections on user-generated content, location data, and rare/protected species.
    </div>

    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <div class="updated">Draft prepared August 2026 · Not yet in effect</div>

    <h2>1. Acceptance of these terms</h2>
    <p>By creating an account or using the Conchquest mobile application ("Conchquest," "the app," "we," "us"), you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, do not use the app. You must be at least 13 years old to create an account.</p>

    <h2>2. What Conchquest does</h2>
    <p>Conchquest provides environmental shelling forecasts (the "Shelling Score"), a shell identification library, and a community feature for logging and sharing shell finds, including location data, photos, and notes.</p>

    <h2>3. Your account</h2>
    <p>You're responsible for keeping your login credentials secure and for all activity under your account. Tell us right away if you believe your account has been accessed without authorization.</p>

    <h2>4. Location data</h2>
    <p>Conchquest uses your device location to generate shelling forecasts for nearby beaches and to let you log finds with GPS coordinates. You control how precisely your location is shared with the community — see our Privacy Policy for details. Exact find locations are never shared publicly by default; you choose whether to share an approximate area.</p>

    <h2>5. Content you share</h2>
    <p>When you post a shell find, photo, note, or comment ("User Content"), you keep ownership of it, but you grant Conchquest a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to host, display, and distribute it within the app and in Conchquest marketing, for the purpose of operating the service. You agree not to post content that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Is illegal, harassing, or infringes someone else's rights</li>
      <li>Reveals another person's exact location without their consent</li>
      <li>Falsely represents a shell's species, rarity, or legal collection status</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Shelling Score is guidance, not a guarantee</h2>
    <p>The Shelling Score and all forecasts are estimates based on tide, weather, and community data. Conditions on the water and the beach can change quickly. You're responsible for your own safety — check official marine and weather advisories, especially during storms, and never enter unsafe surf conditions.</p>

    <h2>7. Shell collection is your responsibility</h2>
    <p>Shell library entries, rarity labels, and regional guidance are provided for educational purposes only. Laws on which shells may be collected — including live shells and protected species — vary by location and change over time. It is your responsibility to know and follow local, state, and federal regulations before collecting. Conchquest is not liable for collection that violates applicable law.</p>

    <h2>8. Subscriptions</h2>
    <p>Premium features are not yet available. Once launched, they will be billed through the Apple App Store or Google Play, managed via RevenueCat. Subscriptions will renew automatically unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the renewal date, through your Apple or Google account settings. Refunds will be handled by Apple or Google per their respective policies.</p>

    <h2>9. Community conduct</h2>
    <p>Be respectful. We may remove content or suspend accounts that harass other users, post spam, misrepresent shell species, or otherwise violate these terms, at our discretion.</p>

    <h2>10. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p>Conchquest is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We do not guarantee the accuracy of tide, weather, or scoring data, which is sourced from third-party environmental data providers and community submissions. The "Shelling Strategy" text summary is generated by a third-party AI provider and may occasionally be inaccurate; it is guidance, not a substitute for the Shelling Score's underlying data.</p>

    <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Conchquest is not liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of the app, including injury sustained while shelling or reliance on forecast data.</p>

    <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms as the app evolves. We'll notify you of material changes in-app before they take effect.</p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms? Reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@conchquest.app">hello@conchquest.app</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <footer class="site-footer-simple">© 2026 Conchquest</footer>
</Layout>

<style>
  .nav-inner-narrow {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .page-wrap {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: 56px 32px 100px;
  }
  .draft-flag {
    background: #fdf1ec;
    border: 1px solid #f3c9b8;
    color: #8a3819;
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .updated {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #9b9a92;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  p,
  li {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #3c3c39;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin: 8px 0 8px;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  a {
    color: var(--teal-deep);
  }
</style>
